@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Switch}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Api}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Switch @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Switch @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api</h1>

<p>
    Everything you need to work with the Switch component: parameters, methods, models, enums, and CSS variables for styling.
</p>

<section class="code-table">

    <h2 id="switch-component-parameters" class="code-table__heading">Switch component parameters</h2>

    <table aria-labelledby="switch-component-parameters">

        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th scope="col">Parameter</th>
                <th scope="col">Type</th>
                <th scope="col">Description</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>Label</td>
                <td>string</td>
                <td>The text displayed to the left of the switch.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>SwitchState</td>
                <td>bool</td>
                <td>Indicates the state of the switch on/off (true/false).</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>AriaDisabled</td>
                <td>bool</td>
                <td>
                    Indicates if the switch is in a disabled state using the <span class="code-span">aria-disabled</span> attribute.
                    <strong>Note: </strong> Both this attribute and the disabled attribute whill have the same styling applied but with <span class="code-span">aria-disabled</span>
                    the switch will still receive focus with the normal focus indicator intact.
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>SpaceBetween</td>
                <td>bool</td>
                <td>
                    The switch is a block element and will take the width of its container, and b default the label will sit next to the switch.
                    Setting SpaceBetween to true will force the label and switch to opposite ends of its container.
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>SwitchStateChanged</td>
                <td>EventCallbac&lt;bool&gt;</td>
                <td>
                    An event raised when the switch is toggled indicating its current state.
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>AdditionalAttributes</td>
                <td>Dictionary&lt;string, object&gt;?</td>
                <td>Sets additional attributes applied to the component's root element.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</section>



<section>
    <h2 class="page-heading">CSS variables defined for the switch component.</h2>

    <p>
        The following sections outline all of the css variables that can be set to alter the styling of the switch component.
        You can of course also override its style classes directly.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Note: </strong> The switch did not really fit the Pane scheme, so rather than try to shoe horn it to fit the variables the majority of the variables do not have
        a shared <span class="code-span">--br-comp-all</span> equivalent.
    </p>
